Note security demo: AES-256 encryption, hashing and safe limits end note.

Note encrypt a message with a key, then decrypt it again end note.
Set message to text meet me at the plain cafe at noon end text.
Set locked to encrypt message with key text our big secret end text.
Say text The locked message is unreadable, and is end text, the length of locked, text characters long. end text
Set unlocked to decrypt locked with key text our big secret end text.
Say text Unlocked it says end text, unlocked.

Note hashing never needs the key back, and cannot be undone end note.
Set stamp to the secure hash of message.
Say text The hash is end text, stamp.
Say text A hash is always end text, the length of stamp, text characters. end text

Note the same text always makes the same hash end note.
Set stamp again to the secure hash of message.
If stamp is equal to stamp again, then
  Say text The hash matched, so the message is unchanged. end text
end if.

Note decrypting with the wrong key fails safely end note.
Try,
  Set junk to decrypt locked with key text wrong key end text.
  Say text This line never runs. end text
if something goes wrong,
  Say text The wrong key was caught safely. end text
end try.

Note secure random numbers come from the system's safe randomness end note.
Set dice to secure random number from 1 to 6.
If dice is at least 1, then
  If dice is at most 6, then
    Say text The secure dice rolled a number from 1 to 6. end text
  end if.
end if.

Note limits keep runaway programs under control end note.
Say text This program stayed inside every safety limit. end text
